xnu 0421: give the LRA its open-loop period before a haptics play

The PBS boost comes up and the play chain clears the fault latch, but the LRA
still reports impedance 0 and does not move. The block's open-loop period,
CFG 0x5c (high nibble) and 0x5d (low byte), has never been written and the two
defines are swapped, so the drive has no oscillation to follow. Program the
live DT's 5882 us period with the vendor's RC-clock factor when the pair reads
zero, as the donor's negroni_haptic.c does. Force VREG-ready only while the
boost is up: bit 1 of VSET belongs to HAP525_HV, which this part is not, and
clearing VSET at stop re-votes the boost rail.

